RuneAudio Wi-Fi setup at boot
=============================

You can use this RuneAudio feature to initially create Wi-Fi profiles or recover a Wi-Fi-only
configuration when you have lost all connectivity.

Create one or more files in the wifi directory which contain the lines:
---
Name=<ssid>
Passphrase=<passphrase>
---

Optionally the following lines can also be added:
---
Hidden=[true|false]
Security=[wep|wpa|wpa1|wpa2|wpa3]
---
The Security parameter is recommended when defining Hidden networks.

Any file name can be used. Use a text editor on your PC to create the files, on the Micro-SD card.
Only lines beginning with 'Name=', 'Passphrase=', 'Hidden=' and 'Security=' will be processed as
parameters. The groups of values can be repeated in a single file or there can be multiple files.
Each time a line is encountered beginning with 'Name=' a new profile is defined. Duplicate valid
parameters occurring without a new network name will be ignored. A Passphrase is required per network Name.
Open networks are ignored. Comments or other text must not be added to parameter lines

There are some example files in the directory /wifi/examples.

This action should be carried out on your PC after inserting the Micro-SD card, the
directory then appears as /wifi, (for Mac users, this is in the first disk partition).

All user created files in the wifi directory will be processed during the RuneAudio startup process. The files will
also be deleted, regardless of the success of the processing. During processing your existing Wi-Fi configuration
will will be left unchanged except for the network names specified in the files in the wifi directory.

If you screw up your network configuration you can also use this function to recreate valid wifi profiles.

By creating a file in the wifi directory your Access Point configuration will also be reset to default values. This
happens regardless of the content of the file (it can be empty).

Example:
---
this line will be ignored
Name=My network name
Passphrase=my P@66w0rd
Hidden=true
Security=wpa2
sometext this line will be ignored
Name this line will be ignored
The lines below will be ignored because these parameters have already been processed fro the previous 'Name='
Passphrase=my 2nd P@66w0rd
Hidden=false
---
